[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Shader Graph & HLSL Fundamentals in Unity"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Welcome to this technical tutorial on blending Unity's visual Shader Graph with custom High-Level Shading Language (HLSL) code. While Shader Graph allows for rapid prototyping, writing custom HLSL code inside Custom Function nodes unlocks limitless mathematical and algorithmic possibilities."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Unity 2022.3 LTS or newer with the Universal Render Pipeline (URP) installed."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Basic familiarity with vector math, normal vectors, and UV coordinates."},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 1: Creating a Custom Function Node"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"To inject custom HLSL into Shader Graph, you need to create a Custom Function node set to 'File' mode or 'String' mode. For reusable logic, the 'File' mode is preferred. Create a new HLSL file in your project assets."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"void MyCustomLighting_float(float3 Normal, float3 ViewDir, out float Out) {
    Out = saturate(dot(Normal, ViewDir));
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 2: Integrating with Shader Graph"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Open your Shader Graph canvas, right-click, and search for the 'Custom Function' node. In the node inspector, reference your HLSL file and specify the function name as 'MyCustomLighting'. Ensure your input and output types match the HLSL signature."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 3: Utilizing HLSL Macros for SRP Batcher Compatibility"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"When writing advanced HLSL functions for URP, you must wrap property declarations inside CBUFFER blocks to ensure SRP Batcher compatibility."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"CBUFFER_START(UnityPerMaterial)
float4 _CustomColor;
float _CustomIntensity;
CBUFFER_END"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining Shader Graph's node-based workflow with custom HLSL blocks, you can maintain clean graphs while executing complex mathematical operations and custom lighting models with optimal performance."}]
